sentences.l:
and his spirit
was warmed, as when about the ears dew
of the crop growing, when the plough-lands bristle;

for you will not fight with the fist, nor will you wrestle,
nor again enter into javelin-throwing, nor on your feet
run;

If only I were so young, and my strength were firm,
as when they were burying lord Amarynceus, the Epeans,
at Buprasium, and the sons of the king set out prizes;

“Atreus’-son and you other well-greaved Achaeans,
two men for these things we bid, who are the best,
with the fist strongly raising them, to strike each other;
